# Stata temp/swap files
*.stswp
~*
*.log
*.smcl

# Stata's own scratch files, named STU<hex>_<hex>.tmp. It writes these beside an output
# during `export excel' and normally removes them; when a do-file errors mid-export it
# does not, and four of them had been committed into outputs/.../tables/ (118 KB) where
# they read as though they were build artifacts.
STU*.tmp

# OS
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini
.DS_Store

# Data files stay in Box, not git
*.dta

# The two inputs that are not ours to publish. Everything else in inputs/ IS tracked, so
# a clone carries the CPI panel's sources and can rebuild everything downstream of the
# crosswalk; these two have to be placed by hand before a rebuild from raw.
#   - the raw market survey is already covered by *.dta above, named here so the rule is
#     legible rather than incidental
#   - the price file comes from a collaborator's NSU_Price.R and carries PSPS price
#     percentiles
# README.md, "Inputs", says which globals point at these and what a clone can still run.
inputs/PSPS NSU Market Survey Launch.dta
inputs/NSU_prices*.csv

# Box Drive sync tombstones, left behind when a file is deleted on the synced drive
*0000000000*

# Python bytecode caches. A .pyc was tracked, so a diagnostic's compiled form showed
# up as a code change on every run that imported it.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# The scratch rebuild verify_pipeline.py writes to compare the crosswalk against a fresh
# build. Regenerated on every run and never read by anything else -- committing it would
# put a second copy of the crosswalk in the repo, which is the ambiguity the comparison
# exists to remove. outputs/tables/build_manifest.json IS committed: it is the reference
# the comparison is made against.
outputs/temp/_verify_rebuild/

# Retired external inputs, kept only so a past question can be re-answered without
# re-sourcing them. Large, externally sourced and re-downloadable, so the bytes stay out
# of git and reference/archive/README.md carries the provenance instead. The README is
# tracked; the data is not.
reference/archive/*
!reference/archive/README.md

# The sandbox validate_folds.do writes to while it is validated against validate_folds.py.
# Holds intermediate .dta files and a second copy of both fold-validation CSVs; the
# canonical pair under outputs/temp/ is what verify_pipeline check 3 reads.
outputs/temp/_folds_port/

# The sandbox 06_cpi_panel.do writes to so its output can be diffed against the published
# CSVs without overwriting them. Regenerated on demand; committing it would put a second
# copy of the CPI panel in the repo, which is the ambiguity the comparison exists to remove.
outputs/temp/_cpi_port/

# Variant builds from an experiment, e.g. 90_diagnostics/measure_anchor_keying.do, which
# sets ${build_name} so the whole build goes to its own subtree instead of overwriting
# the published one. Regenerated on demand and diffed against build; there
# is no reason to keep a second full build in the repo.
outputs/anchor_*/

# The clean from-raw rebuild 90_diagnostics/test_full_rebuild.do writes, for the same
# reason: it is a ~70 MB second copy of the published build, produced to be diffed against
# it and then discarded. The DIFF REPORT it writes is small and does belong in the repo,
# so it goes to outputs/tables/ rather than into this tree.
outputs/test_*/
